{"url": "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/ntu-centennial-fellowship/", "final_url": "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/ntu-centennial-fellowship/", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-24", "text": "Skip to content\n\u53f0\u5927\u570b\u969b\u4e8b\u52d9\u8655\nOpen House\nLearn\nExplore\nFees & Scholarships\nApply\n\u4e2d\nMENU\nHome / Explore / NTU Centennial Fellowship\nNTU Centennial Fellowship\nTo celebrate its centennial anniversary, National Taiwan University proudly introduces the NTU Centennial Fellowship, a prestigious scholarship program for outstanding students from top international partner institutions. This initiative seeks to deepen global academic partnerships, promote cross-border exchange, and support talented individuals in pursuing master\u2019s or doctoral degrees at NTU. Through this fellowship, NTU aims to attract promising international scholars to engage in cutting-edge research and transformative learning, as we embark on the journey toward the next century of excellence. Please check details on the Scholarships page.\nUniversity of Indonesia\nBandung Institute of Technology\nMahidol University\nChulalongkorn University\nUniversiti Tunku Abdul Rahman\nThe Office of International Affairs is here to help! It is our responsibility to ensure that every international student\u2019s needs are met, and that you get the most out of your stay at NTU.\nDrop-in consultation hours: Monday to Friday, 1:30 PM to 4:30 PM\nNational Taiwan University conducts its international student admissions in accordance with the regulations of the Ministry of Education. The University does not collaborate with any study abroad agencies or external institutions for recruitment purposes. Requests from such organizations for campus visits, meetings, or recruitment cooperation are, in principle, not accommodated.\nAll official admissions information is published on NTU\u2019s Overseas Student Admission website. The campus remains open to the public; those who wish to explore are welcomed to visit\u2014no prior application is required.\n7F, Lixian Hall, No 1, Sec 4, Roosevelt Rd, Taipei 10617, Taiwan\n+886-2-3366-2007\nDegree\nBachelor's, Master's, and PhD Admissions\nintadmission@ntu.edu.tw\nDual Degree Programs\nintstudent@ntu.edu.tw\nNon-Degree\nExchange, Visiting,and Research Visiting Programs\nintstudent@ntu.edu.tw\nShort-Term Programs\nntuplusacademy@ntu.edu.tw\n\u00a9 2023 National Taiwan University Office of International Affairs", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/ntu-centennial-fellowship/#primary"], ["\u53f0\u5927\u570b\u969b\u4e8b\u52d9\u8655", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/overseas-students/"], ["Open House", "https://openhouse.ntu.edu.tw/?openExternalBrowser=1"], ["Learn", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/"], ["Colleges & Departments", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/colleges-departments/"], ["English-Taught Programs", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/taught-programs/"], ["Multidisciplinary Learning", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/multidisciplinary-learning/"], ["Future NTU", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/multidisciplinary-learning/future-ntu/"], ["Exchange Programs", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/multidisciplinary-learning/exchange-programs/"], ["Dual-Degree Programs", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/multidisciplinary-learning/dual-degree-programs/"], ["Academic Advising", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/academic-advising/"], ["Learning Chinese", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/learn/learning-chinese/"], ["Explore", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/"], ["Latest News", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/news/"], ["Life on Campus", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/life-on-campus/"], ["NTU Campus", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/life-on-campus/ntu-campus/"], ["Housing & Dining", "https://admissions.ntu.edu.tw/explore/life-on-campus/housing-dining/"], ["Student Clubs", "https://admissions.ntu.e